<section class="lp-sec lp-faq" id="faq"><div class="lp-faq-head" data-anim=""><h2 class="lp-h2">Questions, answered.</h2><p>The short version. Everything else is in the <a href="/docs#faq">docs</a>.</p></div><div class="lp-faq-grid" data-anim="" data-delay="1"><details><summary>Where is my proof built?</summary><p>On your device. The web app builds every zero-knowledge proof in a background worker and the CLI builds it in Node. The relayer only receives the finished proof, never your signature or keys. The first proof downloads a 20 MB proving key once; after that a proof takes a few seconds.</p></details><details><summary>Can the relayer steal or redirect my payment?</summary><p>No. The recipient, the amount and the fee are fixed inside the proof, so changing any of them makes it invalid. The relayer can only submit the transaction or decline to. It pays the gas and is paid by a fee taken from the amount you move.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need gas to send privately?</summary><p>No. The relayer pays gas and the fee is taken from the amount inside the proof. Shielding is the one step paid from your own wallet, because the funds have to come from a public address.</p></details><details><summary>Does Agpool store anything in my browser?</summary><p>No. Nothing goes to cookies, local storage or IndexedDB. Your signature and keys stay in memory and are gone when you close the tab; signing again, on any device, restores the same account.</p></details><details><summary>Which wallets and chains are supported?</summary><p>Any browser wallet, including MetaMask, Rabby, Coinbase Wallet and the in-app browsers of mobile wallets. Pools: ETH and USDG on Robinhood Chain, ETH and USDC on Base and Arbitrum, BNB, USDC and USDT on BNB Chain. Private bridges reach more destinations, Solana included.</p></details><details><summary>Who controls the contracts?</summary><p>Each pool is an upgradeable contract. Its admin can pause or upgrade it but cannot move notes. That admin is a 2-of-3 multisig (Safe) on every chain, so no single key can upgrade or pause a pool. The contracts have not had an external audit yet, so size your balances accordingly.</p></details></div></section>
</template>
